CORE broken-z3-smt-backend no-new-smt
main.c
--cvc5
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ array in union: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ struct array: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ fails: FAILURE$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Reading an array member of a union converts the union's bits to an SMT-LIB
array using (as const ...). CVC5 only accepts a constant value there, and
rejected the formula when that value was the first element of the array.
